-- title:
--   Node places separated by the value of the coordinate y
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring, and $F$ a field extension of $L$ which is a curve over $L$ (every nonzero $f \in F$ has a degree-zero divisor recording its orders $P.\mathrm{ord}\,f$, all residue fields of places are finite over $L$, and $\Omega[F/L]$ is free of rank one) and essentially of finite type over $L$. Let $R_1, R_2$ be regular prolongations of $A$ to $F$ with residue fields $\bar F_1, \bar F_2$ over the residue field of $A$, i.e. valuation subrings $R_i.\mathrm{integers} \subseteq F$ contracting to $A$ on $L$, with surjective residue maps onto $\bar F_i$ whose kernels are the maximal ideals, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero element of $F$ becomes integral with nonzero residue after scaling by a constant; let $x_1, x_2$ be places of $\bar F_1, \bar F_2$ over the residue field of $A$, both rational (the structure map to the residue field of the place is surjective). Let $S$ be a set of places of $F$ over $L$, all rational, and $\mathcal N \subseteq F$ a subring consisting exactly of the elements integral for $R_1$, for $R_2$ and for every $P \in S$; it is assumed that $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$ for $f \in \mathcal N$ and $P \in S$ (here $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ sends an element integral at $P$ to the preimage in $L$ of its residue, and non-integral elements to $0$), that elements of $\mathcal N$ with nonzero $R_i$-residue have that residue of nonnegative order at $x_i$, and that if $f \in F$ has nonzero residue under both $R_1$ and $R_2$ then $\{P \in S : P.\mathrm{ord}\,f \neq 0\}$ is finite with $\sum_{P \in S} P.\mathrm{ord}\,f = x_1.\mathrm{ord}(\bar f^{(1)}) + x_2.\mathrm{ord}(\bar f^{(2)})$. Let $\mathcal N_0 \subseteq \mathcal N$ be a Noetherian local subring such that $S$ is precisely the set of places $P$ at which $\mathcal N_0$ is integral and every non-unit of $\mathcal N_0$ has value in the maximal ideal of $A$, and such that every $f \in F$ satisfies $f b = \sum_{i<n} c_i a_i$ for some $c_i \in L$, $a_i \in \mathcal N_0$ and $0 \neq b \in \mathcal N_0$. Let $C \subseteq A$ be a subring of constants mapping into $\mathcal N_0$, which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with an element $\varpi \neq 0$ such that an element of $C$ has zero residue in $A$ exactly when it is divisible by $\varpi$ in $C$, every element of $A$ being algebraic over $C$; assume further that for $a$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $0 \neq b \in A$ some power $a^n$ is divisible by $b$, and that every element of $\mathcal N_0$ differs from the image of some element of $C$ by a non-unit. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring with irreducible element $\pi$, let $\sigma : W \to \widehat{\mathcal N_0}$ (adic completion at the maximal ideal) send $\pi$ to the image of $\varpi$, let $E \geq 1$, and let $\iota$ be a ring isomorphism of $\widehat{\mathcal N_0}$ with the crossing model $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, W)/(X_0X_1 - \pi^E)$ carrying $\sigma(o)$ to the constant $o$ for all $o \in W$, and such that an element $f \in \mathcal N_0$ whose $R_1$-residue is nonzero of order $n$ at $x_1$ satisfies $\iota(f) \equiv \gamma V^n$ modulo the ideal generated by the constant $\pi$ and $U$ for some unit $\gamma$, and symmetrically with the roles of $R_1, x_1, V$ and $R_2, x_2, U$ interchanged. Finally let $x, y \in \mathcal N_0$ be node coordinates: the $R_1$-residue of $x$ vanishes and its $R_2$-residue has order $1$ at $x_2$, the $R_2$-residue of $y$ vanishes and its $R_1$-residue has order $1$ at $x_1$, and $xy = \varpi^{E_0} u$ for some $E_0 \in \mathbb{N}$ and some unit $u$ of $\mathcal N_0$. Then any two places $P, Q \in S$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,y = Q.\mathrm{evalAt}\,y$ are equal.
--
--   This is the separation (uniqueness) half of the parametrisation of the places lying over a node of a semistable degeneration by the value of a node coordinate: the value $y(P) \in A$ determines the place $P$ of the node annulus. It is used by [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_annulusPair_isAttached_of_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel_of_nodeCoordinates`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_annulusPair_isAttached_of_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel_of_nodeCoordinates) to produce the annulus pair attached to a node.
